    "narrative": {
      "northStar": "The Neural Lab",
      "overview": "Redlin's visual system is a learning science laboratory where intelligence is being forged — not a sanitized dashboard that tracks it. It lives in deep, calm surfaces (navy #1A2A3A, near-black #07141f, light gray #F5F7FA) sliced open by the teal-to-purple gradient that is the product's brand signature. Teal (#20C997) is the dominant voice — it signals action, progress, correctness, and mastery. Purple (#7F63F4) joins it as an equal partner in the gradient, and stands alone as a secondary accent in the study interface. The warm coral (#FF7E67) and amber (#FFB400) provide contrast and warmth in a system that would otherwise read as purely tech-forward.\n\nThe system operates across two visual registers that share one palette and one motion identity:\n\n1. **The Landing (Persuade):** a cinematic, motion-driven, semi-dark surface with hero gradient, floating blobs, and GSAP-staggered hero text. Deep navy background, frosted-glass navbar (backdrop-blur), and bold teal-purple accents fill the viewport.\n2. **The App Shell (Operate):** a light-gray ground (#e9e9e9) with a dark-themed sidebar, light study cards, and teal-purple accents. Sharper, quieter, no radial gradients — the intelligence shows its work through clean structure and precise color rather than spectacle.\n\nThe motion identity is a settled fact: GSAP + Lenis smooth scroll, the WavyBackground ribbon, canvas-confetti on success milestones, and audio cues (button click, card flip, drop card, UI pop) give every interaction physical presence.\n\nThis system actively rejects three aesthetics: no clinical flat-minimal science-tool corporate, no childish gamification (bright candy colors and cartoon hue), and no generic dark-mode-default (the same dark floor). The anti-reference is: not an AI tool that looks like all the other AI tools.",
      "keyCharacteristics": [
        "Teal-first: #20C997 owns the most surface presence — landing CTA, primary app button, selected state, mastery marker, XP indicator.",
        "Dark + light hybrid: the landing lives on deep navy; the app shell on light gray. Both pull from the same palette family.",
        "Gradient as signature: the 135deg teal→purple gradient is the brand symbol — deployed at hero CTA, logo mark, progress bar, mastery milestone, but NEVER as a background wash.",
        "Colored shadows: shadows are sparse here but they glow — teal glow shadows on landing hero buttons and card groups. Every shadow is deliberate, not ambient elevation.",
        "Motion is the continuum: Lenis smooth scroll, GSAP text animation, canvas-confetti on mastery — these are qualities of the identity, not decoration.",
        "Sound presence: four cue mp3s (button click, card flip, drop, pop) + the WavyBackground's canvas wave. Removing sound removes 30% of the system's immediate character."
